TIP:  The intro is the piano part that is played very quickly with two beats per chord.  Prepare by forming (Gadd) with ring finger on the 2nd string and the pinky below it on the 1st string.  Now lift off the 2nd string.  So, two strums of (G), add the ring finger for two strums of (Gadd), lift off the pinky/bottom finger for two strums of (Gadd-), pinky back on for two more strums of (Gadd), lift off pinky again for two strums of (Gadd-), pinky back on for two more sturms of (Gadd), lift off the ring finger for two strums of (G).  Repeat.  

TIP:  If transposing play the (Gadd) root chord and add the 5th note as necessary.  The (Gadd-) may not transpose at all.

TIP:  The Chalypso was a dance popular in 1958.  Yes, I had to look that up.

       
